1
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:14,571
You are a quiet piece of coral resting on white sand ten meters beneath the sea in Australia.

2
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:33,130
Listen closely. That gentle crackle like frying bacon is thousands of tiny snapping shrimp hidden in the reef.

3
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,515
Little blue-striped fish hover above the coral head straight ahead, waiting for a giant visitor.

4
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,169
Look up. Slowly.

5
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,707
A reef manta ray wider than a car is gliding right over your head on silent wings.

6
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,958
Watch its cool shadow slide across the bright white sand beside you.

7
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,852
Manta rays have no sting at all. They are gentle giants of the open reef.

8
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:43,420
Now look straight ahead at the coral tower. The manta slows almost to a stop so the tiny cleaner fish can go to work.

9
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:04,498
They nibble itchy sea bugs right off its skin and even swim safely beside its gill slits.

10
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,626
Look underneath its white belly. Every manta has its own pattern of dark spots, just like your fingerprint.

11
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:54,358
Turn slowly to your left and right. Two more mantas are circling in the blue, politely waiting their turn.

12
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:15,013
And look deeper in the clear water behind them — a green sea turtle paddles calmly past.

13
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:35,042
Everyone shares this one coral station in peace before heading back out to feed in the current.

14
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,667
Above us, winter sunlight shimmers on the surface of the Great Barrier Reef.

15
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:24,127
Watch living reef fishes right now on Tropical reef, Aquarium of the Pacific, and our coral reef cams on Digital Live Zoo.
